In this experiment, I tested two different activation functions: linear and ReLU. With the linear activation function, the neural network could not correctly separate the XOR pattern because it could only learn straight decision boundaries. After changing the activation function to ReLU, the model became capable of learning non-linear patterns. ReLU works by converting negative values to zero while keeping positive values unchanged. This allows the neural network to create more complex decision boundaries and solve the XOR problem.
